<title>USA: Uruguay seeks oil prods to cover '97 refinery work.</title>
<headline>Uruguay seeks oil prods to cover '97 refinery work.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguay's state oil refiner ANCAP is seeking to buy refined products to cover planned refinery work through early April, trade sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>ANCAP is tendering to buy 30,000 cubic meters (188,700 barrels) of gas oil, 8,000 cubic meters (50,300 barrels) of 95-octane gasoline and 2,000 cubic meters (12,600 barrels) of A-1 jet fuel for delivery in early April.</p>
<p>ANCAP is receiving bids Wednesday.</p>
<p>Uruguay normally buys one million barrels of spot crude every four to six weeks, but a planned shutdown of the 34,600 barrels per day (bpd) La Teja refinery through early April has cut near-term needs.</p>
<p>((--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
